      <data key="d2">2b027fe5bbbfb34d51ac16bcd915b8cf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICHAEL S. HART&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">Michael S. Hart was the originator of the Project Gutenberg concept and played a pivotal role in establishing the digital library. He led the creation and distribution of electronic works for over forty years, producing and disseminating free eBooks and significantly contributing to the development of digital access to literature.</data>
      <data key="d2">a22f06338d9771d1617bbf6e0b15d5b8,a33174286d9d6731d658d04ab0089fcc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOUNDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Foundation, specifically the Project Gutenberg Literary Archive Foundation, is a non-profit educational organization based in Mississippi, responsible for managing the mission, donations, and legal compliance of Project Gutenberg."</data>
      <data key="d2">a33174286d9d6731d658d04ab0089fcc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONTCLAIR NJ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Montclair, New Jersey, is the location of the Foundation's business office, serving as a logistical hub for operations."</data>
      <data key="d2">a33174286d9d6731d658d04ab0089fcc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WWW.GUTENBERG.ORG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"WWW.GUTENBERG.ORG" is the official website of Project Gutenberg, serving as the primary portal for accessing its extensive collection of eBooks. The website provides search functions to browse and find digital books, along with donation information to support the organization. Additionally, it offers contact details and subscription options, making it a comprehensive resource for users interested in accessing and supporting Project Gutenberg's digital library.</data>
      <data key="d2">a22f06338d9771d1617bbf6e0b15d5b8,a33174286d9d6731d658d04ab0089fcc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WWW.GUTENBERG.ORG/CONTACT&quot;">
